{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x \\amalg y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(x \\amalg y, w) =\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(x, w) \\times \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(y, w)\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$w$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0c8ccde9fe4733f5f36ebcffb121fc2bf6de1869940e6f04064024058dd6a7c9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdd2804c55652ca13678f609efda95f3d801e1bea362daa230915b5f5f01cf26", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf a coproduct exists it is unique up to unique\nisomorphism. This follows from the Yoneda lemma (applied to the\nopposite category) as\nthe definition requires <MATH_0001> to be an object\nof <MATH_0002> such that\n<MATH_0003>\nfunctorially in <MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9d212167eeb9ad47e963c7b6aafffba3133ff33e795e16be6c830bdfd8790cb", "unit_id": "tag:04AN:prose-0001"}
